          "heading": "Jamie George says Times rift report is 'untrue' ahead of Wallabies",
          "body": "Jamie George says the squad are \"really upset\" by a Times report claiming England's July tour was marked by player unrest over head coach Steve Borthwick's leadership. The report says unhappy players wanted summit talks with Borthwick and RFU chief executive Bill Sweeney in Argentina. \"I can tell you that a lot of it's untrue,\" he told Rugby Union Weekly, querying the timing two days before the Wallabies. George said: \"This is going to galvanise us.\""
