      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Bonus-point win",
          "heading": "Hugo Keenan hat-trick fires Ireland to six-try 42-12 win over Argentina",
          "body": "Friday's win at the Aviva Stadium was built on Hugo Keenan's three tries, but head coach Andy Farrell wanted more. Ireland's six tries also came from Dan Sheehan, Sam Prendergast and Ronan Kelleher, yet they did not score after the 55th minute. \"I thought there was outstanding stuff and some clinical stuff, but I think the story of the game is we missed a chance to be ruthless,\" Farrell said. Robert Baloucoune left with a knock, and Mack Hansen had treatment for an ankle."
        },
